Ryujinx shader translator: AstOptimizer folded a single-assignment value into its uses even when the value is a cross-lane
operation (ballot, vote, shuffle): a unary operation of an operand counts as "worth propagating" for any number of uses, so a
ballot the SASS runs with the whole warp was moved into each use, also into an if that only some lanes enter. There it ran
with those lanes only. Seen in the game's GPU culling (AGENTS.md A18): f2422a7a appends with "VOTE.ALL R13, PT, P0; @lane!=0 skip;
POPC R13 -> ATOMG.ADD count; SHFL base from lane 0; slot = base + POPC(R13 & ltmask)"; the translated code took the ballot
inside the lane-0 branch, so lane 0 reserved one slot per warp while every lane with P0 wrote its record at base + rank: the
records overwrote each other differently every frame (46 records per frame, which ones varied), and the mesh draw counts
after it changed from replay loop to replay loop (foliage flicker). Such a value is now propagated only into the next
statements of the same block with no block in between (the rule spirv-call-args.patch uses for memory reads); otherwise it
stays in its local, computed where the SASS computes it. Applied after spirv-call-args.patch. The Ryujinx code in the
context lines is MIT.
